{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And it came to pass, when he drew near, etc. — Please now, I know, etc.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory said (Bava Batra 16a) that this tells of the modesty that was between them, and it is necessary to understand for what purpose Abraham said this to her." "<b>Indeed</b>, since he wished to command her to say ״he is my brother,״ he was concerned that Sarah might say: why did you bring me into a situation of danger? For in any case she is endangered — either she will be delivered against her will into the hands of the impure through the killing of her husband, or willingly; and he should not have brought her to such a place. And even though the righteous trust in the Holy One blessed be He, nevertheless we have this general principle in our hands: one does not rely on a miracle — and how much more so regarding a person's free choice. And go out and learn (Kiddushin 39b) from Samuel, who said (I Samuel 16:2): ״Saul will hear and kill me.״ Therefore he said to her <b>please now</b>, etc. — he offered an excuse for the matter, for only now did it become known to him and not previously; for had he known what he now knew, he would not have brought her to Egypt and would have gone to another place. And the reason he gave special attention to know, as he approached coming to Egypt — he saw ugly faces, or he knew upon nearing the city that the king would take the most beautiful of the women, and he set his mind and recognized this in her. And his saying ״for she is a beautiful woman,״ etc. — and he did not suffice to say ״for you are beautiful of appearance,״ he intended to say that she is unique in the world: she is a beautiful woman and none compares to her. Understand this." "<b>And let it not</b> be difficult in your eyes that he went with her to the land of the Philistines after he knew that she was a beautiful woman, for the land of the Philistines was not as depraved as Egypt. And therefore you will find that he did not need to command her to say it herself; rather, he said on her behalf ״she is my sister״ (Genesis 20:2), for they did not have a household registry like the people of Egypt, who were at the utmost degree of depravity while she was at the utmost degree of beauty."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:40:53.078634693Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}